      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6brBiV",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3842991186,
      "path": "docs/sequence-diagrams/vaa-eapi-graphql-holidays-document-token-download.md",
      "line": 53,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3842991186",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The diagram describes `retrieveHolidayBookingDocument(documentId, documentToken)` as if `documentId` and `documentToken` are top-level GraphQL arguments, but the implemented contract (and automation payload) uses a single `request` input object (e.g., `retrieveHolidayBookingDocument(request: { documentId, documentToken })`). This should be aligned to avoid misleading API consumers.\n\nThis issue also appears in the following locations of the same file:\n- line 93\n- line 147",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated all three references in docs/sequence-diagrams/vaa-eapi-graphql-holidays-document-token-download.md to show retrieveHolidayBookingDocument(request: { documentId, documentToken }). This matches HolidayQuery.RetrieveHolidayBookingDocument(HolidayDocumentDownloadRequest request, ...) and the automation payload's retrieveHolidayBookingDocument(request: $request) contract."
    }
  ],
